# Association links — “Open” action (backend UI)

Use this pattern whenever the UI shows a **read-only preview** of a **linked / associated record** (person, company, policy, resource, lead, etc.) and offers navigation to the target **admin (backend) screen**.

**Do not** use a plain underlined text `<Link>` or raw `<a>` for the primary “open associated record” action — keep parity with Insurance desk and Resources.

## Required pattern

- **`Button`** with `type="button"`, **`variant="outline"`**, **`size="sm"`**, **`asChild`**
- **`Link`** (Next.js) as the child with:
  - **`target="_blank"`**
  - **`rel="noopener noreferrer"`**
  - **`className="inline-flex items-center gap-2"`**
- **`ExternalLink`** from `lucide-react`: `className="size-4 shrink-0"`, **`aria-hidden`**
- Label: **`t('common.open', 'Open')`** (app locale files already define `common.open`)

## Layout — top-right on the preview “item”

Place the Open control in the **top-right corner of the association preview surface** (card row, dashed preview box, etc.), not below the body copy.

- Wrap the preview block in **`relative`** (the same element that has the card border / padding is fine).
- Position the **`Button`** with **`className="absolute end-3 top-3 z-10 shrink-0"`** (inside a padded card, `end-3 top-3` keeps the control off the border; **`PolicySubjectDetailPreview`** uses `end-0 top-0` on a slightly different shell — both are valid if spacing looks correct).
- Add horizontal reserve on the **main text column** so lines do not run under the button: **`pe-28`** (or equivalent) on the inner wrapper that contains the title / field grid **when** the Open button is shown.
- Omit **`pe-28`** when there is no Open action (e.g. loading or missing `href`).

